  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Newtonian point-mass gravity",
    "positions are DE441 vectors, masses are DE440 GM (the combined effect is measured by the committed validation tests)",
    "m = GM / G, so the source GM is reproduced exactly",
    "each planet with listed moons is its own centre-of-body state (Horizons 399, 599, 699); its mass is the DE440 system GM minus the listed moons, so every planet system keeps its DE440 system GM",
    "moon and planet states come from the same Horizons call (CENTER=500@0), so they share one frame, epoch and origin and no planet-relative transformation is applied"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Earth-Moon, Jupiter and Saturn satellite orbits are Newtonian point-mass orbits: no planetary oblateness, tides or orbital resonance forcing beyond mutual gravity, so the Galilean Laplace resonance and the Moon's apsidal precession are only approximately reproduced",
    "Jupiter and Saturn centre states come from the satellite ephemerides jup365_merged and sat441l (merged with DE441 by Horizons); the Jovian and Saturnian GM of unlisted moons is lumped into the planet",
    "omitted bodies and relativity make the long-term evolution diverge from the real system"
  ],
